[playground-example-outputs  # 202 audited answers, corpus order
 [doc [#
GENERATED — do not hand-edit. Written by
scripts/gen_guide/playground/gen_examples.cx from a grant-free audit run
of every [ex] in examples.cxd, and verified without rewriting by
`make verify-playground-examples` (the generator with --check).
Regenerate with `make playground-examples-regen`.

One [ex] per corpus entry, in corpus order. [out-text] is the child
process's stdout, [err-text] its stderr (emitted only when non-empty),
both as raw-text payloads under the corpus convention: the content
starts on the line after the opening marker and the closing marker sits
on its own line, so exactly one leading and one trailing newline are
the delimiters and not content. That convention normalizes away a final
newline, so `chars=` carries the captured length as measured — a
truncation can never hide behind the payload shape.

An entry marked no-stable-value=true carries no payload: its native
result is a race (see the [no-stable-value] marker in examples.cxd), so
there is no single answer to pin and the sweep asserts only that it
still evaluates. That is the SAME three-state vocabulary
`make test-playground-wasm-eval` grades, not a fourth spelling.

THIS FILE IS THE REVIEW MOMENT. A diff here means an example now
computes something else. Read it against the entry's [note] before
accepting it: a note that promises an answer this file contradicts is
the defect #1170 was filed for.
#]]

